---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { principles } from '../data/principles';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who Antonio Rodríguez Martínez is, how he works, and the principles behind the work: a technical program manager and former CTO who still writes code."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Who I am</h1>
      <p class="hero__intro">
        I'm Antonio Rodríguez Martínez. Technical Program Manager at Stanley Black &amp; Decker, and a
        former CTO. In practice I do product architecture for SBD Digital: specs, user journeys,
        acceptance criteria, and holding the shape of a product across services while a lot of teams
        build pieces of it. I still write code.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="background">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      My work started with a bootstrapped web agency in college, with a friend. We learned to write clean
      code and to manage client projects. A marketing firm acquired us, and I built custom solutions
      under tight deadlines. Since then I have worked as a full-stack developer, architect, CTO, and
      engineering manager, and now as a technical program manager at a global hardware company.
    </p>
    <p>
      Along the way I came to one belief: technical excellence works best with strong team dynamics and
      psychological safety.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="how-i-work">
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      Systems over shortcuts. Humans over hype. I listen and map your reality first, design the smallest
      honest plan, then build, ship, and teach so your team can maintain the work. AI and LLM
      orchestration when it reduces load, not when it adds noise.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="principles">
    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul class="principles">
      {
        principles.map((principle) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
            <p>{principle.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="daily">
    <h2>Daily</h2>
    <p>
      I write almost daily: essays, ideas, documentation. I train: basketball, weights, and martial
      arts. I cook whole foods and parent two kids. I've rebuilt my life post-divorce and learned that
      presence and execution matter more than perfection.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="company">
    <h2>The company</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={SITE.company.url}>{SITE.company.name} LLC</a> is my company. It is the door for
      <a href={SITE.company.consultingUrl}>consulting</a> now and soap later, and it publishes the picture
      books I wrote for my kids. <a href={SITE.notesUrl}>Notes</a> is mine, not the company's.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or on
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/antoniwan" rel="me">LinkedIn</a> and
      <a href="https://github.com/antoniwan" rel="me">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
